diagnosis_text:
A full end-to-end investigation of the reported PC15 ↔ PC16 communication failure found no fault at any layer. Both machines reside on the 172.18.51.0/24 subnet and are connected via switch10 (bridge br0), which in turn uplinks to mswitch2 (br_vlan51). Every component on that path was verified healthy: switch10's bridge has all ten ports in the UP/forwarding state including the exact ports serving PC15 (eth1) and PC16 (eth2); mswitch2's eth2 uplink from switch10 is UP and correctly placed in br_vlan51. Live bidirectional ping tests produced 0% packet loss in both directions (PC15→PC16 and PC16→PC15) with sub-millisecond latency, confirming the data plane is fully operational. ARP tables on both hosts correctly resolve each other's MAC addresses, ruling out any L2 learning problem. Neither machine has any iptables rules — all chains are empty with ACCEPT policy — so there is no host-based firewall blocking traffic. The premise of the helpdesk ticket is false: the network infrastructure between PC15 and PC16 has not failed and no corrective action is required. The users should be advised to check the application layer (file-sharing service, Windows firewall, SMB daemon state) on their machines, as the network path is demonstrably healthy.
=== END ===